{
 "id": "180-9",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "At ORBIT, we take coding standards and consistency very seriously.",
  "It's important for collaboration and maintaining a clean code base.",
  "Take some time to explore, and don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or need clarification on anything.",
  "Remember, my door is always open if you need anything.",
  "We can identify trends and common themes that might not surface otherwise.",
  "First and foremost, it's crucial to create a safe and confidential space for the interview.",
  "We assure the departing employee that their feedback will be kept anonymous and used solely for the purpose of improving our practices.",
  "Building trust is essential.",
  "It's also important to listen actively and empathetically.",
  "We want them to feel heard and understood, so we avoid being defensive or dismissive of their concerns.",
  "Encouraging open-ended questions and creating a dialogue, rather than a rigid question-and-answer session, tends to yield more insightful feedback as well.",
  "While in-person interviews are ideal, we also need to be flexible and respectful of the departing employee's preferences and circumstances.",
  "The key is to adapt our approach while still achieving the main goal of gathering honest and insightful feedback.",
  "Sometimes, employees who are leaving on good terms might be overly positive and not provide constructive feedback because they don't want to burn bridges.",
  "Now, one of the most important things to remember is that an exit interview is just one tool in our toolkit for improving retention and engagement.",
  "Your role as a mentor and as someone who conducts these interviews is crucial to helping ORBIT become an even better place to work.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns along the way."
 ],
